ing 100,000+ residents annually. Population growth directly drives housing demand, keeping vacancy rates low and rents rising.","eco3t":"Job Market Depth","eco3d":"Home to 26 Fortune 500 companies, Houston offers consistent employment across multiple industries. Low unemployment supports tenant stability and reduces default risk for landlords.","eco4t":"Affordable Entry Point","eco4d":"Compared to coastal markets, Houston offers significantly lower price-per-door entry points, allowing investors to build larger portfolios with the same capital — and achieve higher cash-on-cash returns.","finTitle":"Financial Advantages","fin1t":"Strong Cash Flow Potential","fin1d":"Houston's price-to-rent ratios are favorable compared to national averages. Investors regularly achieve 5–8% cap rates and 8–12% cash-on-cash returns, particularly in value-add and BRRRR strategies.","fin2t":"Appreciation + Cash Flow","fin2d":"Unlike many cash flow markets that sacrifice appreciation, Houston delivers both. Median home prices have grown steadily over the past decade while maintaining strong rental yields.","fin3t":"Value-Add Opportunities","fin3d":"Older housing stock in inner-loop neighborhoods offers significant value-add potential through renovation — VanHeight's core business aligns perfectly here.","fin4t":"Short-Term Rental Market","fin4d":"The Texas Medical Center, NRG Stadium, and downtown business corridor create consistent short-term rental demand. Airbnb yields in key zip codes can reach 10–15% gross yield.","taxTitle":"Tax Advantages","tax1t":"No State Income Tax","tax1d":"Texas has zero state income tax. All rental income, capital gains from flips, and business profits are taxed only at the federal level.","tax2t":"Depreciation Shield","tax2d":"Residential rental properties are depreciated over 27.5 years. On a $200K property, that's ~$7,272/year in paper losses that offset rental income.","tax3t":"Cost Segregation","tax3d":"Investors in larger properties can accelerate depre